SUMMARY:Arts and Social Justice Gathering
LOCATION:SHIFT Centre for Social Transformation\, Pavillon J.W. McConnell\,
  1400 de Maisonneuve Ouest (métro Guy-Concordia)
DESCRIPTION:Montréal\n*Le français suit Join us for a day of panels and p
 erformance on arts and social justice. Panels on Arts and Social Justice (
 1:00 – 5:30 pm) Join us for panels at the SHIFT Centre with artists and 
 researchers working on social justice issues. The first panel\, “Artists
  vs. Financialization\,” examines how finance capital threatens the cult
 ural autonomy of artists and undermines their ability to organize collecti
 vely for social change. This discussion also marks the launch of a new zin
 e edited by Brodie Conley and Stefan Christoff. The second panel\, “Cult
 ural Work\, Scholarship\, and the Housing Crisis\,” explores how cultura
 l workers and cultural theorists are creating points of intersection betwe
 en grassroots\, street‑level organizing around the housing crisis and br
 oader struggles for a more…\nOfficial page: https://www.concordia.ca/cue
 vents/artsci/social-justice-centre/2026/10/21/arts-social-justice.html\nR
 ésistance Montréal: https://www.resistancemontreal.org/evenement/arts-an
 d-social-justice-gathering
CATEGORIES:Montréal
URL:https://www.concordia.ca/cuevents/artsci/social-justice-centre/2026/10/
 21/arts-social-justice.html
